---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import ItineraryViewer from '../components/ItineraryViewer.jsx';

// Placeholder: drop the real PDF at public/downloads/ with this name.
const ITINERARY_PDF = '/downloads/valle-de-guadalupe-itinerary.pdf';

// Placeholder gallery slots. Replace each entry with { src, alt, width, height }
// once photos are ready; the aspect ratios here just give the masonry layout shape.
const gallery = [
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[4/5]', label: 'Banyan Tree Veya' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[3/2]', label: 'Vineyards' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-square', label: 'Fauna' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[2/3]', label: 'Golden hour' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[3/2]', label: 'Deckman’s' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[4/5]', label: 'The valley' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[16/9]', label: 'Tasting room' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-[3/4]', label: 'Fire and smoke' },
	{ aspect: 'aspect-square', label: 'Last morning' },
];
---

<MainLayout
	title="Valle de Guadalupe | Steve Bogucki"
	description="Notes from an October 2026 trip to Valle de Guadalupe: Banyan Tree Veya, Fauna, and Deckman’s."
>
	<!-- PLACEHOLDER STORY: replace all narrative copy below with the real write-up. -->
	<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
		<header class="pb-12">
			<p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500">
				Travel · Baja California, Mexico
			</p>
			<h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-zinc-50 sm:text-5xl">
				Valle de Guadalupe
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-pretty text-zinc-400">
				A few days in Mexico’s wine country, organized around a place to stay and two dinners worth
				the drive.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-zinc-500">
				<time datetime="2026-10">October 2026</time>
			</p>
		</header>

		<figure class="mb-16">
			<div
				class="flex aspect-[16/9] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-dashed border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 text-sm text-zinc-600"
			>
				Hero photo
			</div>
			<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">
				The valley in late October, after the harvest.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<div class="space-y-16 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
			<section aria-labelledby="arrival">
				<h2 id="arrival" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">Arrival</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 space-y-5">
					<p>
						The road into Valle de Guadalupe gives you time to slow down. The traffic thins, the
						hills turn to rows of vines, and the pace shifts from schedules to meals. By late October
						the harvest is in and the valley is quieter, which suited the purpose of the trip:
						rest, good food, and very little on the calendar.
					</p>
					<p>
						This is a short account of where we stayed, where we ate, and what stuck with me
						afterward.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="veya">
				<h2 id="veya" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">Banyan Tree Veya</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 space-y-5">
					<p>
						Banyan Tree Veya was home base. The villas sit low against the hillside, so the
						landscape stays the main event, and the design keeps out of the way. Mornings started
						slowly with coffee, a view across the vineyards, and no particular plan until the
						afternoon.
					</p>
					<p>
						What stood out was the restraint. The service was attentive without hovering, and
						the property felt built to make you stay put, which after a long stretch of work was
						exactly the point.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="mt-8">
					<div
						class="flex aspect-[3/2] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-dashed border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 text-sm text-zinc-600"
					>
						Photo: Banyan Tree Veya
					</div>
					<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">Morning at the villa.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="fauna">
				<h2 id="fauna" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">Fauna</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 space-y-5">
					<p>
						Dinner at Fauna was the most deliberate meal of the trip. The menu draws on what the
						region produces, and each course builds on the last. It’s the kind of meal where you
						notice the pacing as much as the plates.
					</p>
					<p>
						Paired with local wine, it made a strong case that some of the most interesting cooking
						in Mexico is happening a short drive south of the border.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="deckmans">
				<h2 id="deckmans" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">Deckman’s</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 space-y-5">
					<p>
						Deckman’s was the counterpoint: open air, wood smoke, and cooking that feels closer to
						the land. Eating outdoors as the light faded over the vineyard was the moment the trip
						came together.
					</p>
					<p>
						If Fauna was precision, Deckman’s was ease. Both were the right call, and I’d book them
						again in the same order.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="mt-8">
					<div
						class="flex aspect-[3/2] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-dashed border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 text-sm text-zinc-600"
					>
						Photo: Deckman’s
					</div>
					<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">Dinner as the sun went down.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="takeaways">
				<h2 id="takeaways" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">Takeaways</h2>
				<div class="mt-5 space-y-5">
					<p>
						The valley rewards planning ahead and then leaving room. Book the dinners early, keep
						the days loose, and let the drive set the pace. The full itinerary is below for anyone
						planning a similar trip.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</article>

	<section aria-labelledby="itinerary-heading" class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-3xl">
		<h2 id="itinerary-heading" class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500">
			Itinerary
		</h2>
		<div class="mt-6">
			<ItineraryViewer client:visible pdfUrl={ITINERARY_PDF} />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="gallery-heading" class="mt-24 border-t border-zinc-800/80 pt-16">
		<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
			<h2 id="gallery-heading" class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500">
				Gallery
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm text-zinc-600">Photos coming soon</p>
		</div>

		<!-- CSS masonry: multi-column layout; items avoid breaking across columns. -->
		<ul class="mt-8 columns-1 gap-4 sm:columns-2 lg:columns-3">
			{gallery.map(({ aspect, label }) => (
				<li class="mb-4 break-inside-avoid">
					<figure>
						<div
							class:list={[
								aspect,
								'flex w-full items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-dashed border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 text-sm text-zinc-600',
							]}
						>
							{label}
						</div>
					</figure>
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
	</section>
</MainLayout>
